//! Error: two incomparable generic overloads tie -- ambiguous
//! Tags: overloads, generics

// Overload ranking has a genericity cost (`int` beats `[T]` beats `T`;
// `param_genericity` in bone-inference), so the bare-`T`-catch-all-vs-concrete
// case now RESOLVES to the concrete overload (positive test:
// tests/overload_genericity_cost.rock). What still ties is a GENUINELY
// incomparable pair: `two(T, int)` and `two(int, T)` each pay exactly one
// bare-hole slot against `(int, int)`, so neither is more specific -- ambiguous,
// and the error lists both tied signatures.

//=== TEST CASE: incomparable_generic_slots_tie_Generic ===
fn two<T>(a: T, b: int) -> string { return "left" }
fn two<T>(a: int, b: T) -> string { return "right" }

fn main() {
    let _ = two(1, 2)
}
